-- Dynamic shell/loader contracts below are documentation, not runtime validation.
-- schema:none means no Rust request deserialiser; it does not mean no params.
-- Rust-backed terminal shell entries name their actual deserialisers.
-- Contract notation: ? optional, | union, [] list; JSON is arbitrary JSON.
-- viud output identity compatibility (2026-11-09): edid_key in display/mode
-- snapshots is now "make model serial @connector:NAME", e.g.
-- "Example Panel 42 @connector:DP-1". Treat it as an opaque preference token:
-- echo the snapshot value for mode/profile requests; never parse or construct it.
-- Legacy EDID-only preference keys remain readable, including "MixOS Headless
-- Unknown" for headless-0 only. Runtime output routing uses connector/protocol
-- names; public comp output slugs are unchanged. An unqualified touch claim on
-- duplicated EDIDs prefers libinput's associated output, otherwise the first
-- matching driven output in existing enumeration order.
-- A qualified output profile overrides its legacy touch claim, including None;
-- association only chooses among outputs that still inherit the legacy claim.
-- If all live candidates override a saved claim, it is unmapped rather than
-- revived by automatic association/size heuristics.
-- All host requests also accept optional output:string and edge:string (default bottom);
-- dispatch validates the edge even for queries. Failures generally rc10, error_code or error,
-- and/or diagnostics; successful acceptance does not prove surface presentation.
-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
-- Copyright 2026 Mark Constable <mc@mixos.dev>
-- Accepted Bus command registry, schema 5. Each component registers its commands
-- here when it enters the tree (AGENTS.md §5). tools/command_registry.mix keeps
-- it canonical: one entry per line, fields in the order name, owner,
-- version, status, class, schema, with no comments inside the commands list. Status is
-- accepted, draft or deprecated; versions are release versions
-- (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH).
--
-- Schema 5 (docs/docs/decisions/2026-10-24-bus-commands-and-actions.md) is
-- schema 4 renamed: the list is `commands` and the registry is the command
-- registry. The fields are unchanged.
--
-- Schema 4 added `schema` to every command and family, last: a serde request
-- type deriving JsonSchema (crate::Type), none (no body or {}), or pending
-- through 2026-11-30 inclusive in UTC. The gate refuses pending after that date.
-- A row may name action::ExecuteRequest only when its command body is exactly {id, params?}; term and the bridged family migrate in later steps.
--
-- Schema 2 added `class` (docs/docs/decisions/2026-10-11-verb-classes.md):
-- intent (changes what a service holds or another caller sees), query
-- (changes nothing another caller could observe; it may write the artefact
-- it returns, as a capture does), input (synthetic low-level input) or
-- system (session plumbing, such as <app>.show). A command the app describes as
-- read_only is a query. When in doubt, it is intent.
--
-- The toolkit drive commands (docs/docs/drive.md) are one family that every egui
-- app answers under its own prefix: <app>.ui.tree, .ui.click, .ui.pointer,
-- .ui.scroll, .ui.key, .ui.type, .ui.menu, .ui.menu.list, .ui.menu.open,
-- .ui.menu.close, .ui.menu.popup, .ui.menu.form, .ui.capture, <app>.window and
-- <app>.window.state. Each native app registers its concrete names, owned
-- by the app that answers them. Schema 3 added the families list below.
-- HELP and app.describe are protocol commands every service answers; they are
-- not registered per component.
-- HELP succeeds at rc 0 with a JSON list of bus::CommandDescriptor objects:
-- {name: string, args: [string], description: string, read_only: boolean}.
-- HELP itself is first; every served command follows once in stable order.
-- read_only is true exactly for registry queries (and protocol discovery).
-- app.describe returns the same list, unless the service documents a richer
-- describe object. Capability discovery does not grant invocation authority.
{
  schema: 5,
  commands: [
